# 🎓 Student Management System (Console-Based)

## 📌 Assignment Overview
This project was developed as part of my academic assignment.

It is a Console-Based Student Management System built using Python.  
The system allows managing student records with role-based access (Admin/User), JSON file storage, and CSV export functionality.

---

## 🎯 Objectives
- Implement CRUD operations (Create, Read, Update, Delete)
- Store student records using JSON file handling
- Export records to CSV format
- Implement grading logic based on marks
- Apply role-based login system
- Practice error handling

---

## 🛠 Technologies Used
- Python
- JSON module
- CSV module
- OS module
- File Handling
- Conditional Statements
- Functions
- Lists & Dictionaries

---

## ⚙️ Features Implemented

### 🔐 Role-Based Login
- Admin login
- User login
- Access control for specific operations

### 📚 Student Record Management
- Add student
- View students
- Update student
- Delete student
- Prevent duplicate roll numbers

### 📊 Grade Calculation System
Marks are converted into grades:

- 90 and above → A  
- 75–89 → B  
- 60–74 → C  
- 40–59 → D  
- Below 40 → F  

### 💾 Data Storage
- Student data is stored in a JSON file.
- Data persists even after the program closes.

### 📤 CSV Export
- Student records can be exported to CSV format.

---

## 📂 Data Structure Used

Student records are stored as a **list of dictionaries**, for example:

```json
[
  {
    "roll": "101",
    "name": "Rahul",
    "marks": 85,
    "grade": "B"
  }
